WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:04.770
- [Reporter] How do you balance
being a player as well as a mother?

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:07.760
- I just, you just do it.

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:09.219
You just get it done and find a way.

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:10.529
What's today, Amaya?

00:00:10.529 --> 00:00:11.396
- Game day!

00:00:11.479 --> 00:00:11.963
- What?

00:00:12.843 --> 00:00:13.944
What is it?

00:00:14.726 --> 00:00:15.811
You look so cute.

00:00:17.903 --> 00:00:20.480
- [Kristen Ledlow]
Motherhood is a 24-7 job.

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:24.313
When the WNBA announced plans for a
bubble of their own, Dearica Hamby

00:00:24.313 --> 00:00:28.960
of the Las Vegas Aces and several
other WNBA players had a difficult

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:33.019
decision to make: opt out of the
upcoming season altogether or opt

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:36.620
in and bring their children into
what's been aptly named the wubble.

00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:38.780
- I didn't think we were gonna
have a season this year.

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:41.850
I was debating on if I was
gonna opt in or opt out.

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:46.239
But once I knew that I was gonna opt
in, I knew Amaya would come with me.

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:48.639
- I wasn't sure if I was gonna bring
her or not because I wasn't sure

00:00:48.639 --> 00:00:52.360
how safe it would be, but actually
going there and being there, it

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:53.959
was as safe as it could be for her.

00:00:55.027 --> 00:00:56.508
Under the water.

00:00:56.516 --> 00:00:57.272
Scrub.

00:00:58.443 --> 00:01:01.290
- [Ledlow] Once inside the wubble
at IMG Academy in Bradenton,

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:04.980
Florida, figuring out that
work-life balance was no easy task.

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:07.920
- [Dearica Hamby] Parenting in
the bubble was an adjustment.

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:09.580
- [Bria Holmes] It's a tough season.

00:01:09.849 --> 00:01:10.830
We're doing pretty well.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:12.340
It's nothing that we wanted to do.

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:14.320
It's just something that
we have to do right now.

00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:17.640
- She's got a lot on
her plate, doing every aspect

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:18.949
of it at a very high level.

00:01:19.539 --> 00:01:24.240
- Some of the kids are able
to be there to experience what this

00:01:24.429 --> 00:01:27.130
wubble, shortened season is like.

00:01:27.759 --> 00:01:29.599
Like how do you keep them entertained?

00:01:29.599 --> 00:01:30.566
[Laughing]

00:01:32.703 --> 00:01:35.113
[Laughing]

00:01:36.414 --> 00:01:40.070
- [Ledlow] When you're in isolation,
where your two main jobs coincide,

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:43.140
finding time for yourself can
be the most challenging part.

00:01:43.799 --> 00:01:46.340
- I will say it is difficult
when I'm taking a pregame nap,

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:49.259
and she's in PE, and they're
hula-hooping and jumping rope.

00:01:49.410 --> 00:01:53.240
And when she's in music class,
and they're doing music, it

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:54.420
can get a little difficult.

00:01:54.590 --> 00:01:55.520
- [Hamby] It was an adjustment.

00:01:55.630 --> 00:01:56.660
You're getting treatment.

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:59.179
You're coming over to
get tested all the time.

00:01:59.179 --> 00:02:01.200
- [Holmes] Shootaround, practice, game.

00:02:01.219 --> 00:02:02.560
Shootaround, practice, game.

00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:04.729
- And then some days, I just wanna sleep.

00:02:04.869 --> 00:02:08.289
- [NAME] It is exhausting to take
care of a three-year-old in life.

00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:10.269
And Dearica is balancing that.

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:12.700
She's balancing playing
at a very high level.

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:15.120
And her daughter, Amaya,
is adorable and precious.

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:16.940
And yet it does take a ton of energy.

00:02:17.429 --> 00:02:19.224
- I mean, you only practice two
hours out of the day

00:02:19.224 --> 00:02:21.359
 but it just seems like
you still have no time.

00:02:21.359 --> 00:02:25.330
But just kind of being able to
find a balance of keeping yourself

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:28.630
sane and also being able to
contribute to your team success.

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:30.720
Also being able to come
back and be a mom helps.

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:34.357
- [Ledlow] Without day care
services, players have to look

00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:35.770
at other means of child care.

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:40.520
Their teammates, friends and
family were ready to step in.

00:02:41.309 --> 00:02:42.459
- My teammates, they love her.

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:44.660
That alone speaks for itself.

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:46.040
- [Hamby] Candace was a big help.

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:46.549
We're neighbors.

00:02:46.790 --> 00:02:48.440
Her and Lailaa spent a
lot of time with Amaya.

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:49.930
- [Candace Parker] Amaya, 
are we friends?

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:50.170
- Yeah.

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:53.920
- [Parker] OK, so, like, real friends
get in an ice bath together.

00:02:54.259 --> 00:02:57.495
- I can stand in front of you
and Bryson can stand here.

00:02:57.495 --> 00:02:59.320
- [Parker] Yes, let's do it. Come on.

00:03:00.065 --> 00:03:04.560
- They just bring so much
joy to everybody in the bubble and

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:06.460
really take the edge off of everyone.

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:08.170
- We got our lucky charm right here.

00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:09.140
[Cheering]

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:11.480
- [Holmes] Just having her here, I
feel like that's my stress relief.

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:14.700
When I'm not having a good day or
being able to just see her grow

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:16.039
every day and be here with me.

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:18.850
We're in this bubble while
I'm still doing my job.

00:03:18.850 --> 00:03:21.399
I mean, it definitely means a lot,
and I'm glad I decided to bring her.

00:03:22.186 --> 00:03:22.898
- Are you dancing?

00:03:23.488 --> 00:03:25.647
- [Hamby] I think I will
remember the experience.

00:03:26.057 --> 00:03:28.765
I think I've learned that it
truly does take a village.

00:03:28.765 --> 00:03:30.101
It takes a lot of people.

00:03:30.113 --> 00:03:31.574
And I think this bubble has shown that.

00:03:31.923 --> 00:03:34.624
- [Parker] To be in a historic
season in the wubble, I think

00:03:34.656 --> 00:03:36.234
we're making the best of it.

